---A Cloud Shell environment, which is defined as the combination of a Docker image specifying what is installed on the environment and a home directory containing the user's data that will remain across sessions. Each user has at least an environment with the ID "default".
---@class gcp.cloudshell_v1.Environment
---@field sshUsername? string Output only. Username that clients should use when initiating SSH sessions with the environment.
---@field publicKeys? gcp.cloudshell_v1.StringList Output only. Public keys associated with the environment. Clients can connect to this environment via SSH only if they possess a private key corresponding to at least one of these public keys. Keys can be added to or removed from the environment using the AddPublicKey and RemovePublicKey methods.
---@field sshHost? string Output only. Host to which clients can connect to initiate SSH sessions with the environment.
---@field webHost? string Output only. Host to which clients can connect to initiate HTTPS or WSS connections with the environment.
---@field id? string Output only. The environment's identifier, unique among the user's environments.
---@field state? gcp.cloudshell_v1.EnvironmentStateEnum Output only. Current execution state of this environment.
---@field sshPort? number Output only. Port to which clients can connect to initiate SSH sessions with the environment.
---@field dockerImage? string Required. Immutable. Full path to the Docker image used to run this environment, e.g. "gcr.io/dev-con/cloud-devshell:latest".
---@field name? string Immutable. Full name of this resource, in the format `users/{owner_email}/environments/{environment_id}`. `{owner_email}` is the email address of the user to whom this environment belongs, and `{environment_id}` is the identifier of this environment. For example, `users/someone@example.com/environments/default`.

---@alias gcp.cloudshell_v1.EnvironmentStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SUSPENDED"|"PENDING"|"RUNNING"|"DELETING"

